==English==

===Etymology===
From {{der|en|frm|collectif}}, from {{der|en|la|collēctīvus}}, from {{m|la|collēctus}}, past participle of {{m|la|colligō|t=I collect}}, from {{m|la|com-|t=together}} + {{m|la|legō|t=I gather}}. Compare {{cog|fr|collectif}}. {{doublet|en|colectivo}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/kəˈlɛktɪv/}}
* {{hyphenation|en|col|lec|tive|caption=Hyphenation, US}}; {{hyphenation|en|col|lect|ive|caption=UK}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɛktɪv}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj|-}}

# formed by gathering or collecting; gathered into a mass, sum, or body; congregated or aggregated
#: {{ux|en|the '''collective''' body of a nation}}
# tending to [[collect]]; forming a collection
#* {{rfdatek|en|Young}}
#*: Local is his throne {{...}} to fix a point, / A central point, '''collective''' of his sons.
# having plurality of origin or authority
# {{lb|en|grammar}} expressing a collection or aggregate of individuals, by a singular form
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} deducing consequences; reasoning; inferring.
#* {{RQ:Browne RM}}
#*: critical and '''collective''' reason

